{
  "$comment": "Machine-readable canonical vocabulary for Game Production OS. Markdown documents explain these terms; this file is the single source for names and machine-checkable rules. tests/validate_framework.py checks that schemas and documents agree with it. Changes follow core/GOVERNANCE.md. Per gate: permitted_owners may record the gate; default_review_policy applies unless routing or project authority sets another permitted policy; acceptable_evidence counts toward PASS; base_evidence.all_of must all be present and at least one of base_evidence.any_of (if non-empty); each conditional_evidence entry applies when routing applies its condition id, adding its requires types and, if requires_context is set, requiring at least one counting evidence of the gate's base types captured in one of those contexts; insufficient_alone may be attached as support but can never alone support PASS; evidence captured in non_counting_contexts does not count, except where context_scope_exceptions allows it for listed scope kinds. evidence_context_compatibility lists the capture contexts in which each evidence type can exist at all; any other combination is invalid (schema-enforced). decision_ref_fields lists every field that references a Human Decision and the decision kinds it may resolve to (Phase-2 referential integrity). decision_payloads defines the structured value each decision kind must carry; decision_value_bindings lists, for each decision reference, which config value (relative to the object holding the reference, or absolute when it starts with /) must equal which decision field \u2014 a decision of the right kind but a different value does not authorize the config. record_id_uniqueness lists identifiers that must be unique within a project record set; JSON Schema cannot enforce uniqueness by property, so record-set validation must reject duplicates before any lookup. decision_subject_rules states which subject a decision must have when it authorizes a configuration value. decision_may_omit in a binding lets a decision be broader than the record (e.g. no revision = any revision of that scope). Evidence counts for a gate only when evidence.subject equals the gate scope (kind and ref) or an accountable evidence_applicability entry maps it. Gate records produced for a routed task carry routing_ref and must agree with their routing entry. workflow_gate_requirements lists each workflow's invariant gates (always_required) and the gates routing adds when affected; review_policy_strength orders policies for the effective-policy rule. cross_review_eligibility maps each owning skill to the specialists whose passing review may close its gate. platforms is the target-platform vocabulary shared by project config and evidence provenance; target-runtime evidence counts only on a declared project target platform, DEVICE_EVIDENCE only on a declared reference device where the platform lists any, and release_primary_platform_coverage lists the evidence each PRIMARY platform needs for release.",
  "gpos_version": "1.0.0-alpha.7",
